# Secured and Monitored Web Infrastructure

## Infrastructure Diagram
https://github.com/ixhadeel/holbertonschool-system_engineering-devops/blob/main/web_infrastructure_design/2-secured_and_monitored_web_infrastructure.png

## Security
- Three firewalls protect the load balancer and the two application servers.
- An SSL certificate is installed on the load balancer to serve www.foobar.com over HTTPS.
- HTTPS encrypts traffic between the user and the load balancer.

## Monitoring
- Three monitoring clients collect metrics and logs from the three servers.
- The monitoring service receives the collected data for analysis.
- To monitor web server QPS, measure the number of HTTP requests handled per second.

## Infrastructure Issues
- SSL termination at the load balancer means backend traffic may remain unencrypted.
- Only one MySQL server can accept writes, which creates a write availability risk.
- Having the same components on all servers can cause resource contention and make scaling harder.
